IMPORT prelude

-- Local Forces (Relief of Financial Hardship) Act 1953 (Singapore) -- what counts as a local force (s 2, s 6 and the Schedule), to
-- whom and to what service the Act applies (s 3), the entitlement to relief for financial hardship arising out of service (s 4), the
-- annulment of rules by Parliament (s 5(3)) and the duty to consult the civil defence Minister (s 7).
--
-- Edition: 2020 Revised Edition, as deposited at ../../registers/source-bundle/LFRFHA1953.txt. The deposit says it "incorporates
-- all amendments up to and including 1 December 2021 and comes into operation on 31 December 2021"; the last amending law in its
-- Legislative History is Act 24 of 2004 (Police Force Act 2004, in force 12 October 2004), and the Schedule is annotated [24/2004].
--
-- WHY THIS ACT. Requirement REQ-0183 in subjects/sg/requirements.jsonl: Tier 3 of the remaining Singapore Acts, ordered by
-- everyday-life relevance. The requirement asks what the Act decides for a person it applies to; no scenario has asked a sharper
-- question yet. The Act is seven sections long, so the whole of its operative text is encoded.
--
-- NOT ENCODED: the rules made under s 5 (none were deposited, and the amount, conditions and procedure for relief live there); the
-- content of the Gazette notifications under ss 3 and 6 (none were deposited -- appointed dates are inputs here); the rule-making
-- heads in s 5(2)(a)-(f) beyond noting that they exist; the meaning of "actual service", "active service" and "full-time service",
-- which the Act leaves to "any written law relating to that force".
--
-- NAIVE ENCODING. Straight from the deposited text with the writing-l4-rules conventions of the example rows. No pipeline, no
-- coverage table, no independent test pass, no human gate. NOT for public use. See NOTES.md.

§ `Local Forces (Relief of Financial Hardship) Act 1953`

DECLARE Force IS ONE OF
    `the Singapore Civil Defence Force`
    `the Special Constabulary`
    `the Singapore Armed Forces`
    `the Vigilante Corps`
    `the regular Singapore Police Force`
    `a private security agency`

DECLARE ServiceKind IS ONE OF
    `actual service`
    `active service`
    `full-time service`
    `duty without being called out`

DECLARE Sufferer IS ONE OF
    `the member himself`
    `the member's wife`
    `the member's child`
    `another dependant of the member`
    `a relative who is not a dependant`

DECLARE MinisterPower IS ONE OF
    `appointing a date under s 3`
    `declaring cessation under s 3`
    `making rules under s 5`
    `amending the Schedule under s 6`
    `a power under another Act`

§§ `2, 6 and the Schedule -- local forces`

-- s 2: "'local force' means any force specified in the Schedule". The Schedule lists: 1. the Singapore Civil Defence Force (Civil
-- Defence Act 1986); 2. the Special Constabulary (Part 8 of the Police Force Act 2004); 3. the Singapore Armed Forces (s 7 of the
-- Singapore Armed Forces Act 1972); 4. the Vigilante Corps (s 3 of the Vigilante Corps Act 1967).
-- s 6: "The Minister may, by notification in the Gazette, from time to time as he may think fit add to or delete from the list".
-- The regular Police Force is NOT in the Schedule; only its Special Constabulary is.
GIVEN `the force` IS A Force
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the force is listed in the deposited Schedule` IF
    CONSIDER `the force`
    WHEN `the Singapore Civil Defence Force` THEN TRUE
    WHEN `the Special Constabulary` THEN TRUE
    WHEN `the Singapore Armed Forces` THEN TRUE
    WHEN `the Vigilante Corps` THEN TRUE
    OTHERWISE FALSE

GIVEN `the force` IS A Force, `added by notification` IS A BOOLEAN, `deleted by notification` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the force is a local force` IF
        (`the force is listed in the deposited Schedule` `the force` AND (NOT `deleted by notification`))
    OR  ((NOT `the force is listed in the deposited Schedule` `the force`) AND `added by notification`)

§§ `3 and 4(2) -- to whom and to what service the Act applies`

-- s 3(1): the Act "shall apply to any member of a local force who is called out for actual service, active service or full-time
-- service under the provisions of any written law relating to that force, but only from such date as the Minister may, by
-- notification in the Gazette, appoint". (2): "different dates in respect of different local forces".
-- (3): the Minister may declare that the Act "shall cease to apply to members of any local force ... from and after such date as may
-- be appointed therein, but the declaration shall be without prejudice to any right of relief arising out of the service of those
-- members before that date".
-- s 4(2): "'service' means actual service, active service or full-time service in a local force on and after the date appointed
-- under section 3(1)".
-- Days are counted as plain numbers on one calendar; the appointed and cessation days are those notified for THIS force.
GIVEN `the kind` IS A ServiceKind
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the kind of service qualifies` IF
    CONSIDER `the kind`
    WHEN `duty without being called out` THEN FALSE
    OTHERWISE TRUE

GIVEN `is a member of a local force` IS A BOOLEAN,
      `the kind` IS A ServiceKind,
      `a date has been appointed for the force` IS A BOOLEAN,
      `appointed day` IS A NUMBER,
      `cessation declared for the force` IS A BOOLEAN,
      `cessation day` IS A NUMBER,
      `service day` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the service is service to which the Act applies` IF
        `is a member of a local force`
    AND `the kind of service qualifies` `the kind`
    AND `a date has been appointed for the force`
    AND `service day` AT LEAST `appointed day`
    AND ((NOT `cessation declared for the force`) OR `service day` < `cessation day`)

§§ `4(1) -- entitlement to relief`

-- s 4(1): "Any person to whom this Act applies shall be entitled in accordance with any rules made under section 5 to relief in
-- respect of financial hardship suffered by him or his wife or children or other dependants and arising out of his service."
-- The Act fixes no amount and no conditions; s 5(2)(b), (c) leave "the circumstances in which and the conditions under which" and
-- "the amount of such relief" to the rules. So the entitlement is encoded as conditional on the rules providing for the case.
-- The claim day is deliberately NOT an input: s 3(3) preserves "any right of relief arising out of the service ... before" the
-- cessation date, so a claim made after cessation turns only on when the service was rendered.
-- The text names "his wife"; whether a husband of a female member falls within "wife" or only within "other dependants" is not
-- settled by the deposit (see NOTES.md). A non-dependant relative is outside the list.
GIVEN `the sufferer` IS A Sufferer
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the sufferer is within s 4(1)` IF
    CONSIDER `the sufferer`
    WHEN `a relative who is not a dependant` THEN FALSE
    OTHERWISE TRUE

GIVEN `the Act applies to the service` IS A BOOLEAN,
      `the sufferer` IS A Sufferer,
      `financial hardship was suffered` IS A BOOLEAN,
      `the hardship arose out of the service` IS A BOOLEAN,
      `rules under s 5 provide for the case` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the member is entitled to relief` IF
        `the Act applies to the service`
    AND `the sufferer is within s 4(1)` `the sufferer`
    AND `financial hardship was suffered`
    AND `the hardship arose out of the service`
    AND `rules under s 5 provide for the case`

§§ `5(3) -- annulment of rules by Parliament`

-- s 5(3): every rule shall "as soon as possible after the making thereof, be presented to Parliament and if, at the next sitting of
-- Parliament after the order is presented to it, a resolution is passed annulling the rule or any part thereof, the whole rule or
-- such part thereof ... shall thenceforth be void but without prejudice to the validity of anything done thereunder."
-- ("the order" is the text's word, though the instrument is a rule.)
-- Annulment is effective only if passed at the NEXT sitting after presentation; "thenceforth" is read as from the day of the
-- resolution onward (an inference about the boundary day).
GIVEN `annulled at the next sitting` IS A BOOLEAN, `annulment day` IS A NUMBER, `the day` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the rule is void on the day` IF
    `annulled at the next sitting` AND `the day` AT LEAST `annulment day`

GIVEN `annulled at the next sitting` IS A BOOLEAN, `annulment day` IS A NUMBER, `day of the act done` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `an act done under the rule stays valid` IF
    NOT `the rule is void on the day` `annulled at the next sitting` `annulment day` `day of the act done`

§§ `7 -- consultation on the Civil Defence Force`

-- s 7: "The powers conferred upon the Minister by sections 3, 5 and 6 shall not be exercised so as to affect the Singapore Civil
-- Defence Force ... or any member of that Force, without previous consultation with the Minister charged with the responsibility for
-- civil defence." The "Minister" of the Act is the Minister for defence (s 2).
GIVEN `the power` IS A MinisterPower
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the power is one of ss 3, 5 and 6` IF
    CONSIDER `the power`
    WHEN `a power under another Act` THEN FALSE
    OTHERWISE TRUE

GIVEN `the power` IS A MinisterPower, `affects the Civil Defence Force or its members` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `prior consultation with the civil defence Minister is required` IF
    `the power is one of ss 3, 5 and 6` `the power` AND `affects the Civil Defence Force or its members`

GIVEN `the power` IS A MinisterPower,
      `affects the Civil Defence Force or its members` IS A BOOLEAN,
      `the civil defence Minister was consulted first` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the exercise complies with s 7` IF
        (NOT `prior consultation with the civil defence Minister is required` `the power` `affects the Civil Defence Force or its members`)
    OR  `the civil defence Minister was consulted first`
